    <p>I set up Playwright CI integrations frequently. What looks like a 20-minute task ("just add a GitHub Actions workflow") usually takes two to three hours when you account for dependency caching, parallel execution configuration, artifact upload, and the inevitable debugging of the first few CI failures that don't reproduce locally.</p>
    <p>This post covers the setup I use for most engagements, with the decisions explained so you understand why, not just what to copy.</p>

